**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleEditorWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WindowLauncherTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`

**How to implement.** Pinned replaces VersionsInUse (001 §C 'Versions are immutable', 'Pinned replaces VersionsInUse'; .spec-md §0.1 `Lifecycle.fs` row, §5 `PinState`, §6 'Version rule'). A pin is one-way and belongs to one version; it is set through a store verb, and nothing derives 'in use' from live experiments any more. This is one step because deleting the seam's type changes every caller at once. `PinState` (`VersionPinned` / `VersionUnpinned`, with `value` and `tryOfDb`) is step 61's and is reused, never declared again (ELEV014/016). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Lifecycle.fs`: `VersionsInUse` (`Lifecycle.fs:VersionsInUse`, with `empty`), `VersionUsage` (with `ofBool`) and `usageOf` are deleted. `decideVersioning`'s last parameter becomes `(pin : PinState)`, the stored latest version's pin, and its table reads: physics identical and metadata identical is `KeepCurrent`; physics identical and metadata changed is `MutateInPlace`, whatever the pin; physics changed is `MutateInPlace` when `VersionUnpinned` and `MintNextVersion` when `VersionPinned`. 001 §C binds 'edit latest' to this rule, so a pinned version's physics never changes in place, and a kit's snapshot hash is the second safeguard. Its doc table says pinned / unpinned. `VersionRef` stays, because an experiment still binds a sample by version (`Experiments.fs:ElementBinding`); its doc drops the in-use sentences. The module doc names the pin where it named the seam. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs`: `MaterialProxy` gains `pinMaterialVersion : MaterialVersionId -> Result<unit, MaterialError>`, after `supersedeMaterial`. Its doc list gains the verb (a pin is one-way), `saveMaterial`'s entry says it decides with the latest version's pin, and `removeMaterial`'s says it refuses a material with any pinned version. `MaterialVersionInUseErr` becomes `MaterialVersionPinnedErr of reason : string`, and its doc says removal is refused while any version is pinned. The `VersionNumber` and `MaterialVersionId.firstOf` docs say pinned where they say used and drop their `VersionsInUse` and 'step 25' clauses. Directly after `MaterialVersionId`, `type MaterialError with static member unknownMaterialVersion (version : MaterialVersionId) : MaterialError` holds the one text for an unresolved material version, moved from `Propagation.fs:resolveMaterialVersion` (`unknown material version '<id>' v<n>`), which now calls it, so the pin verb below reuses it (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'); its doc is one line citing spec 0050 S2.2. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs`, the same for samples: `SampleProxy` gains `pinSampleVersion : SampleVersionId -> Result<unit, SampleError>`, after `supersedeSample`; `SampleVersionInUseErr` becomes `SampleVersionPinnedErr of reason : string`; and the `SampleError`, `SampleProxy`, `SampleVersionId.firstOf` and `samplesReferencing` docs, with the comment above `samplesReferencing` (`ElementId.fs:1044-1050`), say pinned and drop the seam. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialStore.fs` and `SampleStore.fs`: each version record gains `pin : PinState`. A new id inserts version 1 `VersionUnpinned`, and a minted version starts `VersionUnpinned`; `MutateInPlace` and the three lifecycle verbs keep the version's pin. `saveMaterial` / `saveSample` pass the latest version's pin to `decideVersioning`, and `usageAt` is deleted. `pinMaterialVersion` / `pinSampleVersion` set `VersionPinned` on the named version and answer `Ok ()`, also when it is already pinned; an id the store does not hold, or a version its history does not hold, is `MaterialError.unknownMaterialVersion` / an `UnknownSampleIdErr` naming the id and the version as `v<n>`. No verb unpins. `removeMaterial` keeps its referenced-by-samples refusal first, then refuses a material with any pinned version as `MaterialVersionPinnedErr`, whose reason keeps today's shape (the name, the id, the count and the versions as `v1, v2`) with 'pinned' in place of 'bound by a live experiment'; `removeSample` refuses likewise with `SampleVersionPinnedErr`. `createInMemory` loses its `versionsInUse` parameter: `MaterialProxy.createInMemory (samplesReferencing : MaterialId -> Sample list)` and `SampleProxy.createInMemory ()`. The module and member docs say pinned. (5) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`: `boundVersions` and `versionsInUseSeam` are deleted. `ElementBinding.versionRefOpt` and `Experiment.versionRefs` stay, because they say what an experiment binds; their docs name no seam, and the `Lifecycle` open's comment names `VersionRef` alone. `ExperimentCollectionStore.fs`'s module doc drops its clause about the app-scope `VersionsInUse` source. `CatalogueImport.fs` (step 37), `createInMemory`, builds `SampleProxy.createInMemory ()` and `MaterialProxy.createInMemory (samplesReferencing samples)`, and its material and sample reason matches name the renamed cases. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` the comments above the `Lifecycle.fs`, `Experiments.fs` and `SampleStore.fs` items lose the clauses naming `VersionsInUse`, `boundVersions` and `versionsInUseSeam`; nothing is added (AGENTS.md: no new comments in project files). (6) Ui. `ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs` (`MaterialError.caption`, `SampleError.caption`) and `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:runFailureCaption` name the renamed cases. The comments that describe a used version or the seam say pinned or drop the clause: `LibraryWindowView.fs:selectedVersionsOf`, `MaterialsWindowView.fs:selectedVersionsOf`, the `AddLayerClicked` and `SaveClicked` comments of `SampleEditorView.fs`, and `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:descriptorBinding`. `AppContext.fs:AppContext.create` builds its stores through `CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory` since step 44 and needs no change. (7) Every caller, with one rule. A call that passes a `VersionsInUse` value drops it, and so does the fixture: `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore (samplesReferencing : MaterialId -> Sample list)` and `BuiltinCatalogue.sampleStore ()` (step 45); every caller of these and of the two `createInMemory`s follows. A fact that stubbed the seam with versions builds the plain store and pins those versions through the new verb. Every stub `MaterialProxy` record gains `pinMaterialVersion = fun _ -> Ok ()` and every stub `SampleProxy` record `pinSampleVersion = fun _ -> Ok ()`: in `MaterialProxyTests`, `SampleProxyTests`, `MaterialEditorWindowTests` (two), `MaterialsWindowTests`, `SampleEditorWindowTests` (three) and `LibraryWindowTests`. An `open OpticalConstructor.Domain.Lifecycle` whose only use was the seam goes, with its comment; so does the `VersionsInUse` clause of the `LifecycleTests.fs` item comment in `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`, whose 'used/unused' becomes 'pinned/unpinned'. The callers at authoring time are the constructor suite's `CategoryProxyTests`, `MaterialProxyTests`, `SampleProxyTests`, `LifecycleTests`, `ExperimentProxyTests`, `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests`, `PropagationTests`, `SourceLibraryTests`, `BuiltinCatalogueFixtureTests` and the fixture `BuiltinCatalogue.fs`, and the UI suite's `EmbeddedChartTests`, `FsxAcceptanceTests`, `InverseConstructorTests`, `LibraryWindowTests`, `LightSourceEditorTests`, `MainWorkbenchTests`, `MaterialEditorWindowTests`, `MaterialsWindowTests`, `OutOfBandBadgeTests`, `SampleEditorWindowTests`, `ScrollExtentTests`, `SolverHandoffWindowTests`, `WindowLauncherTests`, `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`. A caller the closing grep finds anywhere else is re-pointed by the same rule. (8) Facts. `LifecycleTests`: the helper `decide` takes a `PinState`, and the eight decision-table facts keep their expectations under their pinned names: `identical save keeps the current version — unused` becomes `identical save keeps the current version — unpinned`; `identical save keeps the current version — used` becomes `identical save keeps the current version — pinned`; `metadata-only edit never versions — unused mutates in place` becomes `metadata-only edit never versions — unpinned mutates in place`; `metadata-only edit never versions — used mutates in place, does NOT mint` becomes `metadata-only edit never versions — pinned mutates in place, does NOT mint`; `unused physics change mutates in place` becomes `unpinned physics change mutates in place`; `used physics change mints the next version` becomes `pinned physics change mints the next version`; `unused physics-and-metadata change mutates in place` becomes `unpinned physics-and-metadata change mutates in place`; `used physics-and-metadata change mints the next version (new metadata rides along)` becomes `pinned physics-and-metadata change mints the next version (new metadata rides along)`. `usageOf reports VersionUsed for a ref the seam contains and VersionUnused otherwise` and `a bound version unlocks the used-version rule through the seam` are deleted with their subject. The module doc and the section comment say pin. `MaterialProxyTests` and `SampleProxyTests`: `proxyWithUsed` becomes `proxyWithPinned`, a fresh store whose listed versions are pinned through the verb, and `v1Ref` goes. The facts that used it keep their expectations: `KeepCurrent — an identical save on a used version leaves exactly version 1 unchanged` becomes `KeepCurrent — an identical save on a pinned version leaves exactly version 1 unchanged`; `MutateInPlace — a metadata-only edit of a USED version updates version 1 and does NOT mint` becomes `MutateInPlace — a metadata-only edit of a PINNED version updates version 1 and does NOT mint`; `MutateInPlace — a physics change of an UNUSED version updates version 1 in place` becomes `MutateInPlace — a physics change of an UNPINNED version updates version 1 in place`; `MintNextVersion — a physics change of a USED version freezes version 1 and mints version 2` becomes `MintNextVersion — a physics change of a PINNED version freezes version 1 and mints version 2`; `removeMaterial on a material with a used version is blocked with a typed refusal naming the version` becomes `removeMaterial on a material with a pinned version is blocked with a typed refusal naming the version`; `removeMaterial succeeds when the material is neither sample-referenced nor version-used` becomes `removeMaterial succeeds when the material is neither sample-referenced nor pinned`; and in `SampleProxyTests`, `KeepCurrent — an identical save on a used version leaves exactly version 1 unchanged` becomes `KeepCurrent — an identical save on a pinned version leaves exactly version 1 unchanged`; `MutateInPlace — a metadata-only edit of a USED version updates version 1 and does NOT mint` becomes `MutateInPlace — a metadata-only edit of a PINNED version updates version 1 and does NOT mint`; `MutateInPlace — a structure change of an UNUSED version updates version 1 in place` becomes `MutateInPlace — a structure change of an UNPINNED version updates version 1 in place`; `MintNextVersion — a structure change of a USED version freezes version 1 and mints version 2` becomes `MintNextVersion — a structure change of a PINNED version freezes version 1 and mints version 2`; `removeSample on a sample with a used version is blocked with a typed refusal naming the version` becomes `removeSample on a sample with a pinned version is blocked with a typed refusal naming the version`; `removeSample succeeds when no version is in use, then the id is unknown` becomes `removeSample succeeds when no version is pinned, then the id is unknown`. The STUB facts' refusals name `MaterialVersionPinnedErr` / `SampleVersionPinnedErr`, and `a sample layer keeps resolving its pinned material version after the material mints a newer one` pins `MaterialVersionId.firstOf MaterialIds.glass152` through `pinMaterialVersion` where it stubbed the seam. `MaterialProxyTests` gains `pinMaterialVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused`: pinning version 1 of `MaterialIds.glass152` twice answers `Ok ()` both times; a physics change (the `MaterialIds.glass200` complexity) then mints version 2; a second physics change, back to the original complexity, mutates version 2 in place, so no version 3 resolves and version 1 keeps the original physics; and pinning version 1 of a freshly minted id, and version 3 of `MaterialIds.glass152`, answer `UnknownMaterialIdErr` naming the id and the version. `SampleProxyTests` gains `pinSampleVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused`, the same over `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` and the `SampleIds.glassPlate2mmId` structure. `ExperimentProxyTests`: `boundVersions collects the versioned bindings of the setup (samples yes, presets no)` becomes `versionRefs collects the versioned bindings of the setup (samples yes, presets no)`; `a bound version appears in versionsInUse and BLOCKS removal of that sample` becomes `pinning an experiment's bound sample version BLOCKS removal of that sample`; `editing a USED sample version mints the next version instead of rewriting it` becomes `editing a PINNED sample version mints the next version instead of rewriting it`. The first asserts on `e1.versionRefs`; the other two pin each `SampleVersionRef` of `e1.versionRefs` through `pinSampleVersion` of `BuiltinCatalogue.sampleStore ()`, and the second still removes the sample freely from a store nothing pinned. `committing from a scene captures the ordered chain including the detector kind` and `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests`' `createInMemory round-trips a collection of E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving ordered setups, optional shapes, and DataFilePath attachments` read the experiment's `versionRefs` where they read `boundVersions`, with the same expected references.

**Acceptance.** After the replacement, `git grep -n -E "VersionsInUse|versionsInUse|VersionUsage|VersionUsed|VersionUnused|usageOf|boundVersions|versionsInUseSeam|VersionInUseErr" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged (the two deleted LifecycleTests facts out, the two pin facts in), including `pinMaterialVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused`, `pinSampleVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused` and the renamed decision-table, removal and ExperimentProxyTests facts; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the ten s09 invariants MUST pass.
